.TH NEVERBALL 1
.SH NAME
neverball \- tilt a level to guide a rolling ball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B games/neverball
[
.B -d
.I directory
]
[
.B -l
.I level.sol
|
.B -r
.I replay.nbr
]
[
.B -n
.I frames
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Neverball
runs Neverball 1.6.0 in a rio window.
Tilt the floor to collect enough coins and reach the goal before time
runs out, without falling off the level.
.PP
The mouse or arrow keys tilt the floor.
Enter activates menu items; Escape goes back or pauses play.
R restarts the level when available.
The 1, 2 and 3 keys select camera modes; E cycles them, and S and D
rotate the camera. F9 toggles the frame counter and F12 saves a PNG.
The window may be resized during play, retaining its logical aspect ratio.
.PP
The menus select level sets, balls and replays, and edit the player name.
Settings, scores and recordings are stored separately from Neverputt's.
.PP
.B -d
selects the game data directory.
.B -l
loads a compiled level directly, without selecting a set.
.B -r
plays a recorded game.
.B -n
exits after the specified number of displayed frames and reports the
average frame rate, including rendering, readback and window presentation.
.PP
Original assets are installed on the host by
.BR boot/getneverball .
In the native source directory,
.B mk data
compiles missing maps and decodes Ogg audio into 44.1 kHz stereo PCM.
Neverball and Neverputt use the same assets and native platform code.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /sys/games/lib/neverball
Original data and generated maps/audio for both games.
.TP
.B $home/lib/neverball
Settings, log, Screenshots, Replays and Scores.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/games/neverball
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR neverputt (1),
.IR audio (1),
.IR tinygl (2),
.IR gpu (3)
.SH BUGS
Requires a VirtIO GPU with VirGL and its host-owner access.
The native port supports mouse and keyboard, English menus and a rio window;
fullscreen display modes, gamepads, VR, reflections and multisampling are
not provided.
